<title>USA: USDA donates farm commodities to Russia.</title>
<headline>USDA donates farm commodities to Russia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture said Friday it was donating $260,000 of U.S. farm products to Russia under the Food for Peace program.</p>
<p>The commodities, including 125 tonnes of wheat flour, 150 tonnes of vegetable oil, 150 tonnes of rice and 75 tonnes of white beans, would be distributed through Chamah, a private voluntary organization.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8394</p>
